  The entries below come from the tracing agent in conditional mode with `com.alibaba.druid.**` as user code. I kept Druid's lookups of its own classes and resources plus the `org.slf4j.Logger` probe, and left out the JDK management beans and H2 entries that the agent also files under Druid classes. `MockDriver` is there because the druid jar lists it in `META-INF/services/java.sql.Driver` next to `DruidDriver`, so `DriverManager` loads it. With these entries the native output is the same as the JVM output. Only the slf4j backend and the `stat` filter were exercised. The other backends and filters are looked up the same way.
  
